// LegalRuleML 1.0: the graph model and sample data
//
// Generated by ../../cypher.py from model.json and sample.json. Edit those and regenerate, rather than this file.
//
// A LegalRuleML document modelling four sections of a fictional Residential Tenancies (Example) Act 2024 of Victoria.
// A strict rule obliges the tenant to pay rent on time, repaired by a late fee penalty; a defeasible rule obliges the
// landlord to give 28 days' notice to vacate, with two alternative readings, and is overridden by a defeasible rule
// permitting 14 days' notice where the premises are unfit; a further rule prohibits the landlord from entering
// without notice. Associations tie each statement to its section, the enacting authority, the jurisdiction and its
// in-force date, and the agents, figures and roles of the tenancy and of the drafting are recorded beside them.
//
// Run it against an empty database of Neo4j 5 or later, Enterprise Edition, for its node key and property existence
// constraints, e.g. with cypher-shell -f model.cypher. It merges every node and relationship, so it can be run again.

// The model: its constraints

